## How to Use This Document
Distinguish confirmed requirements an implementation AI can follow from matters that must remain on hold until confirmed.
Mark an item resolved only when confirmed statements in specifications 01-07 provide one unambiguous, consistent answer, and state the supporting evidence.
Do not treat missing statements, implicit guesses, or repeated proposals as confirmation. Do not authorize the implementation AI to adopt unresolved choices independently.

## Unresolved Items
Create a table of item IDs, subjects, statuses (TBD, Needs confirmation, or Unadopted proposal), reasons for remaining unresolved, questions to confirm, affected scope, and related specification and requirement IDs.
Map each item to a relative link such as [03_data.md](03_data.md), a section name, and requirement IDs, quoting the necessary statements.
Keep existing options labeled as proposals. Do not invent an adopted option, decision maker, deadline, or numeric value.
Keep independent questions separate and distinguish implementation work that depends on a decision from work that can proceed without it.
If there are no unresolved items, state "No unresolved items" and the scope reviewed. Do not invent issues to meet an item count.

## Items Resolved by the Specifications
Show the original question, statements establishing the answer, referenced Markdown files, sections and requirement IDs, and the reason for resolution.
If a reference marked To be defined in a later stage is now defined in a later specification, cite both the original reference and the definition.
Determine resolution from the supplied statements. Do not claim resolution by adopting a recommendation or filling in missing design details.

## Cross-Specification Conflicts and Pending Decisions
Show both conflicting statements and their references, the impact, and questions requiring confirmation. Leave the decision pending.
Do not favor a statement because it appears more often or in a later-generated specification. Leave requests for original-source verification open when needed.

## Consistency and Open Questions
For each file in 01-07, make the reviewed sections, corresponding item IDs, and resolved or outstanding status traceable.
Record missing evidence, further confirmation sources, and the confirmation order implied by dependencies.
Do not claim to have inspected the original source. Treat quotations in earlier specifications as quotations from those specifications.
